<title>USA: Target Therapeutics gets FDA OK for coil.</title>
<headline>Target Therapeutics gets FDA OK for coil.</headline>
<dateline>FREMONT, Calif 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Target Therapeutics said it received clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA), to market its Guglielmi Detachable Coil (GDC).</p>
<p>The coil is used for minimally invasive treatment of vascular lesions through arterial and venous embolization in the peripheral vasculature.</p>
<p>With this FDA action, Target can market the GDC for neuro and peripheral indications such as aneurysms, arteriovenous malformations, arteriovenous fistulas, lesions and tumors in disease sites accessible through small blood vessels.</p>
</text>
